From 6c0f910c52c5715c3211c3e123ed09d23a6f89c9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ParkerrDev <114211845+ParkerrDev@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 22:44:04 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] xwayland: add xwayland:scale, one scale for X11 clients on
 every monitor

X11 has a single coordinate space and a single DPI for all its clients, so
an X11 client cannot be given the scale of the monitor it is on. X11 apps
either render at 1 and are upscaled, or with force_zero_scaling render at
each monitor's pixels and need every toolkit told the scale by hand.

xwayland:scale is the one scale every X11 client renders at: -1 the highest
monitor scale rounded up to a whole number, -2 the highest as it is, or a
number. An X11 window is then pixel for pixel on a monitor of that scale
and downscaled, with linear filtering, on lower ones.

With an Xwayland that binds xwayland_shell_v1 version 2, the scale is sent
to it with a logical layout and Xwayland shows its windows at their logical
size itself, so X11 surfaces need no special handling. With an older one,
Hyprland lays the X11 screen out at the scale and scales the windows.

CX11Backend now tells the X11 scale (client geometry, size hints) apart
from the scale its surfaces come in at, and reportedSize() is in the
surface's coordinates. The version 2 protocol XML is vendored until a
wayland-protocols release has it.
